      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hi There,\n\nTested & Confirmed issue. Crashed few seconds after joining. Was running Proton-GE 8.19 on VRC Open Beta.\n\nCPU: AMD R9 5950X 16C/32T\n\nRAM: 64GB DDR4 @ 3600\n\nGPU: NVIDIA RTX 3090 (Driver Ver: 535.113.01-2)\n\nDistro: Arch Linux + KDE 5.27.8 + Wayland\n\nKernel Version: 6.5.7-zen2-1-zen\n\nMore testing may be required if it's just a world issue or if AVPro is causing issues again.\n\nNOTE: This post will be edited for more tests.\n\n2nd Test World: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_dd2bd994-851e-4b94-83b6-9b03547c67bd\n\n- This world has AVPro and works fine.\n\n3rd Test World: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_860bdea8-0499-4c16-8170-5683a3a3ab8a\n\n- Also works fine\n\n- Performed picture taking and no issues or lag either.\n\n4th Test (Same world from 2nd Test)\n\n- Crashed w/ only 4 cores/threads available via running \"for x in /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu{4..31}/online; do echo 0 | sudo tee $x; done\" to artificially create lower-end system or steam deck\n\n(Suggested by galister in \"linux vr adventures\" discord)\n\nNOTE 2: I'm unsure if steam deck uses Wayland or X11 so results may vary depending on that. SteamOS on the deck is based on arch and uses KDE desktop environment if I remember correctly.\n\nHope this helps.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
