  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "After the 2023.3.3p1, AvPro worlds now violently crash shortly after entering, 100% of the time.\n\nI followed these steps on Deck, they're an exert from the link below.\n\n1. Create an Invite+ instance of Show Talents game show world , https://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_20f170b0-57b4-4673-a8a7-329ebc07e047\n\n2. Join instance, pressing `Go` on loading if needed\n\n3. Walk out the elevator towards the show stage (opening door with button if needed)\n\n4. Wait for the video to load and play as shown on the media controls at the back of the stage (VRChat may need to download the YouTube-DL executable)\n\n5. **If on desktop, force a desynchronization between audio and video** with anything that causes VRChat to briefly stutter - **any or all of the following steps might work**\n\nTo trigger the crash, try:\n\n- Take a high-res photo with the camera\n\n- Toggling on the Personal Mirror\n\n- Switching avatars\n\nTested on Deck with:\n\n- Default Proton, VRC Stable\n\n- Proton Experimental, VRC Stable\n\n- Default Proton, VRC Beta\n\n- Proton Experimental, VRC Beta\n\n(stable is 1358, beta is 1370)\n\nCrash behavior was same in all cases.\n\nThis seems to plague the Deck as well as Linux users in general, the issue has been very well documented by the Linux VR community here, with additional info and logs:\n\nhttps://github.com/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/1199#issuecomment-1770336669",
